e Unstructured.io platform and API designed to transform unstructured documents (such as PDFs, emails, and forms) into clean, structured JSON output[1][2][3].\n\n### Key Concepts\n*   **Purpose:** Unlike standard partitioning, which converts files into generic document elements, the `structured_data_extractor` allows you to define a specific target JSON schema[2]. It then extracts only the precise data fields you require from your source files[4][2].\n*   **Methods:** It supports two primary subtypes for extraction[5][3]:\n    *   **LLM (Large Language Model):** Uses language models to extract data based on a provided JSON schema or plain-language extraction guidance[6][2].\n    *   **Regex:** Uses regular expression patterns to identify and extract specific data, such as prices or ID numbers[7][8][3].\n\n### Usage in the API\nWhen using the Unstructured API, the `structured_data_extractor` is typically configured as a node within a job's processing pipeline[9][5]. \n\n**Example Configuration Snippet:**\nIn API requests, you define the extractor within the `job_nodes` array[9][10]:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Extractor\",\n  \"type\": \"structured_data_extractor\",\n  \"subtype\": \"llm\",\n  \"settings\": {\n    \"schema_to_extract\": {\n      \"json_schema\": { ... },\n      \"extraction_guidance\": \"...\"\n    },\n    \"provider\": \"openai\",\n    \"model\": \"gpt-5-mini\",\n    \"output_mode\": \"extracted_data_only\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### How to Access\n*   **API/SDK:** You can integrate the extractor programmatically using the Unstructured Python SDK or by sending requests directly to the Unstructured API[9][3].\n*   **UI:** It is also available via the Unstructured workflow designer and the Start page for local file processing[5][3].\n\nSources:\n[1] [unstructured.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHMVxQSLAkSWIHWBCQHcbvZAabNz26Nn4K1KfeOCiKoGbiCXh2xmGYVzCH6JccGv20KIi4D2OCQohuGPCdbpkor9WZjBXtwJNsCteiMXyv40J18pKgAKJzdYkNb1Q