{"step_index":1250,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:26:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:26:58+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:27:00+03:00\nThe search for \"\"unstructured-transform-client\" pypi\" returned the following summary:\nThe `unstructured-transform-client` is a Python package available on PyPI that serves as a client for the **Unstructured Transform v2 API**[1][2].\n\n### Key Details\n*   **Purpose:** It is designed to facilitate the conversion of unstructured files (such as PDFs, emails, images, and scanned documents) into structured data[2][3][4]. This structured output is optimized for use in AI applications, vector databases, and other downstream data pipelines[3][4][5].\n*   **Functionality:** The library handles tasks like document partitioning, enrichment, chunking, and embedding[3][4].\n*   **Integration:** It is closely related to the broader \"Unstructured\" ecosystem, which provides tools for ingesting and preprocessing complex documents for LLMs (Large Language Models)[4][6].\n\n### Note on Usage\nWhile `unstructured-transform-client` exists as a specific package for the Transform v2 API[1], official documentation for Unstructured's operations and SDKs often references the `unstructured-client` package (e.g., `pip install \"unstructured-client>=0.46.2\"`) for general API interactions[7]. \n\nIf you are looking to integrate document processing into AI agents, you may also encounter the **Unstructured Transform MCP (Model Context Protocol) server**, which allows AI agents to interact with the Unstructured Transform platform using standard protocols[3][4][8].\n\nSources:\n[1] [getsafety.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFcMUzK7IauwwLIMCnaeQe_kCGsA4CJ2wu1J23F1XEUyKbm_ZIaOz7rIzMFYhbKF7OQNiGjHm7RhmPndJk7vZKeTfpfJwpJy3SCd7GCMjefL7mXx1ZCzuiiyywIgeLOzDgn5N1h4TaHSliLETe243zi2IQD4SdKCQ==)\n[2] [getsafety.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-ap