{"step_index":1279,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T01:28:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:28:44+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:28:44+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.system_generated/tasks/task-1277.log`\nTotal Lines: 841\nTotal Bytes: 18482\nShowing lines 1 to 800\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: \"\"\"The public surface: `client.parse.run(...)`, `client.extract.run(...)`.\r\n2: \r\n3: \r\n4: \r\n5: WHY A FACADE AT ALL\r\n6: \r\n7: ───────────────────\r\n8: \r\n9: openapi-generator produces `ParseApi(api_client).parse_run(...)` across four\r\n10: \r\n11: unrelated Api classes. That is not the surface openapi.yaml says we ship — the\r\n12: \r\n13: spec declares `tags` + `x-sdk-method-name` per operation precisely so the call\r\n14: \r\n15: reads `client.parse.run(document)` (decision N1, API v2 Surface Proposal), and\r\n16: \r\n17: no generator reads those. This module is where that declaration becomes real.\r\n18: \r\n19: \r\n20: \r\n21: It also supplies three things the generator cannot:\r\n22: \r\n23: \r\n24: \r\n25: 1. `extract.from_document(...)`. POST /api/v2/extract declares BOTH an\r\n26: \r\n27:    application/json body (ExtractRequest, the parse_id flow) and a\r\n28: \r\n29:    multipart/form-data body (ExtractDocumentRequest, the raw-document flow).\r\n30: \r\n31:    openapi-generator emits only the first and drops the second without a\r\n32: \r\n33:    warning — ExtractDocumentRequest is absent from the generated models\r\n34: \r\n35:    entirely. One of the three launch flows, silently missing, in both Python\r\n36: \r\n37:    and TypeScript. It is reconstructed here over the generated transport.\r\n38: \r\n39: 2. `jobs.stream(...)`. The SSE progress stream the service really serves.\r\n40: \r\n41: 3. `schema=` instead of `var_schema=`. The generator renames the field to dodge\r\n42: \r\n43:    Pydantic's `BaseModel.schema()`; the wire name stays `schema` via an alias,\r\n44: \r\n45:    so only the Python signature is ugly. Callers should never see it.\r\n46: \r\n47: \r\n48: \r\n49: The method names here are not free-form: `tests/test_facade_matches_the_spec.py`\r\n50: \r\n51: reads openapi.yaml and asserts this module exposes exactly the calls the\r\n52: \r\n53: contract declares. The spec stays the source of truth; this file is held to it.\r\n54: \r\n55: \"\"\"\r\n56: \r\n57: \r\n58: \r\n59: from __future__ import annotations\r\n60: \r\n61: \r\n62: \r\n63: import json\r\n64: \r\n65: import os\r\n66: \r\n67: from typing import Any, Iterator\r\n68: \r\n69: from urllib.parse import quote, urlencode\r\n70: \r\n71: \r\n72: \r\n73: from . import _host_headers\r\n74: \r\n75: from ._generated.api.extract_api import ExtractApi\r\n76: \r\n77: from ._generated.api.jobs_api import JobsApi\r\n78: \r\n79: from ._generated.api.parse_api import ParseApi\r\n80: \r\n81: from ._generated.api.upload_api import UploadApi\r\n82: \r\n83: from ._generated.api_client import ApiClient\r\n84: \r\n85: from ._generated.configuration import Configuration\r\n86: \r\n87: from ._files import FileInput, as_file_part\r\n88: \r\n89: from ._generated.models.extract_request import ExtractRequest\r\n90: \r\n91: from ._multipart import post_multipart\r\n92: \r\n93: from ._retry import RetryConfig, call_with_retries\r\n94: \r\n95: from ._sse import JobEvent, stream_job_events\r\n96: \r\n97: \r\n98: \r\n99: DEFAULT_SERVER_URL = \"https://transform.unstructured.io\"\r\n100: \r\n101: \r\n102: \r\n103: # Matches the service's own security scheme names; see openapi.yaml's\r\n104: \r\n105: # `securitySchemes` and the generated Configuration.auth_settings.\r\n106: \r\n107: _API_KEY_HEADER = \"unstructured-api-key\"\r\n108: \r\n109: _API_KEY_ENV_VAR = \"UNSTRUCTURED_API_KEY\"\r\n110: \r\n111: \r\n112: \r\n113: \r\n114: \r\n115: class TransformClient:\r\n116: \r\n117:     \"\"\"A client for the Unstructured Transform v2 API.\r\n118: \r\n119: \r\n120: \r\n121:     Pass an API key or bearer token explicitly, or leave both out to read\r\n122: \r\n123:     `UNSTRUCTURED_API_KEY`. Both credential types are accepted by the service\r\n124: \r\n125:     and whichever you send is forwarded upstream verbatim, so an API key and a\r\n126: \r\n127:     bearer token are not interchangeable in what they authorise — they are two\r\n128: \r\n129:     different identities, and sending both would leave which one is in force up\r\n130: \r\n131:     to the server's precedence rules rather than your intent.\r\n132: \r\n133:     \"\"\"\r\n134: \r\n135: \r\n136: \r\n137:     def __init__(\r\n138: \r\n139:         self,\r\n140: \r\n141:         *,\r\n142: \r\n143:         api_key: str | None = None,\r\n144: \r\n145:         bearer_token: str | None = None,\r\n146: \r\n147:         server_url: str = DEFAULT_SERVER_URL,\r\n148: \r\n149:         send_host_headers: bool | None = None,\r\n150: \r\n151:         user_agent_suffix: str | None = None,\r\n152: \r\n153:         timeout_seconds: float | None = None,\r\n154: \r\n155:         retries: RetryConfig | None = RetryConfig(),\r\n156: \r\n157:     ) -> None:\r\n158: \r\n159:         # An explicit credential always wins. A bearer token is intentionally\r\n160: \r\n161:         # independent from the API-key environment variable: callers who pass\r\n162: \r\n163:         # one have made an explicit authentication choice.\r\n164: \r\n165:         if api_key is None and bearer_token is None:\r\n166: \r\n167:             api_key = os.environ.get(_API_KEY_ENV_VAR) or None\r\n168: \r\n169: \r\n170: \r\n171:         if (api_key is None) == (bearer_token is None):\r\n172: \r\n173:             raise ValueError(\r\n174: \r\n175:                 \"pass exactly one of api_key or bearer_token, or set \"\r\n176: \r\n177:                 f\"{_API_KEY_ENV_VAR} — they are different identities, not \"\r\n178: \r\n179:                 \"interchangeable spellings of one credential\"\r\n180: \r\n181:             )\r\n182: \r\n183: \r\n184: \r\n185:         self._server_url = server_url.rstrip(\"/\")\r\n186: \r\n187:         self._timeout_seconds = timeout_seconds\r\n188: \r\n189:         self._retries = retries\r\n190: \r\n191: \r\n192: \r\n193:         configuration = Configuration(host=self._server_url)\r\n194: \r\n195:         if api_key is not None:\r\n196: \r\n197:             configuration.api_key[\"ApiKeyAuth\"] = api_key\r\n198: \r\n199:             self._auth_headers = {_API_KEY_HEADER: api_key}\r\n200: \r\n201:         else:\r\n202: \r\n203:             configuration.access_token = bearer_token\r\n204: \r\n205:             self._auth_headers = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {bearer_token}\"}\r\n206: \r\n207:         # urllib3 has its own Retry layer underneath the generated client. Keep\r\n208: \r\n209:         # retry decisions in this facade so non-idempotent submit safety and\r\n210: \r\n211:         # Retry-After caps are applied consistently.\r\n212: \r\n213:         configuration.retries = False\r\n214: \r\n215: \r\n216: \r\n217:         self._api_client = ApiClient(configuration)\r\n218: \r\n219: \r\n220: \r\n221:         if timeout_seconds is not None:\r\n222: \r\n223:             self._apply_default_timeout(self._api_client, timeout_seconds)\r\n224: \r\n225:         self._apply_retries(self._api_client, retries)\r\n226: \r\n227: \r\n228: \r\n229:         # Identification headers, per TRNSFRM-91. Set as ApiClient defaults so\r\n230: \r\n231:         # every generated call carries them without each namespace remembering\r\n232: \r\n233:         # to; the SSE path is not a generated call, so it merges the same dict\r\n234: \r\n235:         # itself rather than relying on that.\r\n236: \r\n237:         self._client_headers = _host_h